{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI-INFRASTRUCTURE NOTE — a Verified -1 / Code-Review -1 pair appeared on patch set 2 of BOTH\nchanges that was NOT a test failure and NOT the pip-audit blocker. Recording the mechanism so the\nnext agent does not misread it as a real regression or re-do the work.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED: runs 30772712323 (change 1240) and 30772713254 (change 1241) both ended\nconclusion=CANCELLED, and in both the `build-and-test (gate + suite on the patchset)` job was\nSKIPPED, not failed — `clear-vote` was cancelled early, so everything downstream skipped or\ncancelled. The `vote` job runs `if: always()`, so it still cast Verified -1 (and Code-Review -1)\noff a run that never executed a single test. A cancelled run is therefore INDISTINGUISHABLE from a\ngenuine failure by the vote alone; the run's job list has to be read to tell them apart.\n\nWHY: .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:40-43 sets\n    concurrency:\n      group: gerrit-verify-${{ github.event.inputs.GERRIT_CHANGE_ID || github.run_id }}\n      cancel-in-progress: true\nThe run history shows dispatches arriving in near-simultaneous PAIRS 1-2s apart, with the earlier\nmember of each pair killed when the next pair queues — i.e. under this session's multi-agent load\nthe group is not isolating per change the way the comment above it (\"a newer patchset for the same\nchange cancels the in-flight run\") intends. Consequence worth knowing: rechecking two stacked\nchanges in the same breath is self-defeating, and a recheck can also cancel ANOTHER agent's\nin-flight run. Serialize rechecks on a stack; do not fire both at once. I did not touch the\nworkflow (out of scope, and it is a repo-wide condition, not this ticket's).\n\nRESOLUTION: the stale votes were cleared automatically and a fresh run (30772783956) started on\nits own — no further recheck was needed, and I deliberately did not post another one rather than\nadd to a contended queue and risk cancelling someone else's run.\n\nREAL SIGNAL SO FAR: on the last run that actually executed the suite, the ONLY non-pip-audit\nfailure was the docs/env-vars.md drift gate, which patch set 2 fixes. Every other job was green:\nlint + type-check, module-size gate, artifact provenance, golden-path clean install, both\noptionality jobs, eval discipline, ticket resolvability, whole-store authorship."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785714314006707001,"uuid":"dcf808b4-cccd-4643-942c-6269ecff07ba"}